Start the companion's neighbour map renders one per frame instead of all at once (cell change hitch fix).

companion-localmap-export.patch makes LocalMap::requestMap also render every loaded neighbour segment
that has no map yet, so the companion screen shows the whole 3x3 grid. Each of those is a camera that
draws the whole scene from above, and on an outdoor cell change all of them (up to 5 on a diagonal
step) were set up in the same frame as the player's own cell. Measured on a Retroid Pocket Duo Lite
with the DSPerf probe and simpleperf: the frame after a cell change took 110-230 ms in render, and the
local map cameras plus their readback were a large part of it.

The neighbours are now queued. LocalMap::cleanupCameras, which the window manager calls every frame,
starts at most one of them per frame, and none in a frame that already started a map render. A queued
segment is skipped if its cell has left the grid, got its map from a normal request, or the player is
inside by then.

